hey don't end up meeting  in Britannia  although s Connor doesn't seem fully  aware of where they are in reality  Merlin allows s Connors consciousness to  meet with Rosa in the afterlife inside  the capital of the Dead this confirms  that Rosa died sometime after a skinner  left his home Kingdom perhaps during the  barbarian invasion s Canora thanks Rosa  for protecting him all those years ago  and he promises to live his life to the  fullest in order to honor her sacrifice  s Canora promises to do the right thing  by Rosa no matter how lonely and awkward  he might be and Rosa tells him that he  has always done right by her and that he  doesn't need to feel alone anymore this  reunion is true  a heartwarming moment but it is also a  sad moment because s Kannur doesn't seem  to realize why Rosa hasn't aged and why  she has been watching over him this  whole time s Kannur doesn't seem to  realize that Rosa is dead nevertheless  he promises Rosa that even though he  almost abandoned this life he is now  going to devote his life to his precious  friends and now we know what promise s  Connor was talking about back in Chapter  three to seven it seems that he wasn't  talking about a promise he made two mile  or meliodas  which are the two options that I was  thinking of when I first read the  chapter rather he seems to be referring  to the promise he made to Rosa the  promise about dedicating his life to his  friends and this reinforces the  possibility that s kannur may be  intending to sacrifice his life for his  friends in the fight against the demon  king but if this is as Connors plan it  would go against the main lesson that  has been so prevalent in this side story  the idea that s can or cannot abandon  his life so easily that he must live on  in order to honor the sacrifice that  Rosa made for him so is this kind of  really about to push his body to the  breaking point in order to reach a state  beyond the one and defeat the demon king  is this decision going to actually cost  him his life in the end or is this kind  were going to survive thanks to the help  of his friends the sins remember'd a  scene from the Side Story that I talked  about earlier the scene in which  malleolus defeats a scanner and then  tells him that if he ever loses control  meliodas will be there to stop him from  going berserk and hurting himself or  others I can't help but think that this  might be foreshadowing for what is about  to happen next in the epic fight against  the demon king is meliodas going to  realize that s Kannur is pushing himself  too far and that he is about to die and  his meliodas then going to use his full  demon lord powers to knock askin or out  in order to save him from himself  s Connor seems determined to give up his  life for his friends but as we saw in  the side story s Connors friends don't  want s Kannur to die they want him to  live and I'm wondering if the only way  to stop asking her from overdoing it  will be to literally knock him out in  the middle of the fight against the  demon king we will have to wait and see  but to me the main message of the side  story is that s Kenard needs to value  his life more and that he needs to be  willing to rely on his friends he seems  to always want to protect others at his  own expense  but perhaps the wiser strategy would be  to work together with his friends  instead of sacrificing his own life in a  one-on-one battle with the demon king I  have to say that I truly appreciate Eska  nor as a character including the  dichotomy between his daytime and  nighttime personalities and the fact  that this power that he received through  no fault of his own the divine grace  sunshine might be a blessing in the  sense that it makes him probably the  strongest human who has ever lived but  it is also a curse because it condemned  him to a life of loneliness and misery  at least in the early stages of his life  before he met the sins on the one hand  we have a daytime Eskin or who says that  kings are as plentiful as grains of sand  but there is only one s Kannur and on  the other hand we have a nighttime s  Connor who doesn't even think that he  deserves to live at least at first  s canora's life has been tragic in so  many ways but the one bright spot in his  life has been Merlyn and the other sins  his precious friends he now seems  committed to sacrificing himself for his  friends and that may lead to the tragic  end of his life but I have a feeling  that his friends will step in and  especially manly Otis in order to stop  Eskin or from sacrificing himself  I certainly hope that s kannur survives  because after everything that we know  about his tragic past he deserves a  happy ending his plan might be to give  up his life for his friends  but I hope his plan fails or changes  because I want to see us gonna live and  to be completely honest I want to see  the relationship between s Cara and  Merlyn develop in the side story it is  implied that Merlyn is also lonely that  she has lonely eyes just like Rosa and s  Kannur we don't actually know a lot  about Merlin's past and we really need a  side story for her too in order to learn  more about her but I have always been  rooting for Merlin and s kannur to end  up together I think their personalities  would complement each other well and I  think that after living in loneliness  for such a long time they both deserve  to be happy together in conclusion even  though s Connor has led a tragic life  and even though there are clues to  suggest that s Canora might be about to  give up his life for his friends  I really hope that s Koerner will have a  happy ending rather than a tragic one  but let me know what you guys think is s  Kannur about to push himself too far and  die or is something else going to happen  let me know down in the comments I  always love hearing from you if you  enjoyed this video you want to see more  seven deadly sins content right here on  the  please leave a like to let m